To resolve the security vulnerabilities identified in your scan, you need to update the flagged packages to their latest secure versions. Based on the provided image image_2.png, the vulnerable packages are react-router-dom (version ^7.7.0), @vitest/ui (version ^4.0.7), and vite (version ^7.0.4).
Update Commands
Run the following commands in your project's root directory to force an update to the latest versions.
 * Update the production dependency:
   npm install react-router-dom@latest

 * Update the development dependencies:
   npm install -D vite@latest @vitest/ui@latest

(Note: If you use yarn or pnpm, replace npm install with yarn add or pnpm add, respectively).
Verification Step
After running the installation commands, verify that the vulnerabilities have been resolved by running:
npm audit

If the command reports 0 vulnerabilities, the update was successful.
Required Code Changes
Whether you will need to make code changes depends on the versions that get installed:
 * No changes likely needed (Patch/Minor update): If the security fix was released as a minor or patch update (e.g., updating from 7.7.0 to 7.7.1), your existing code should work without any modifications.
 * Changes might be needed (Major update): If the latest secure version is a new major release (e.g., jumping from 7.x.x to 8.x.x), there might be breaking changes.
To ensure everything works after upgrading, run your test suite (npm run test) and check that your application still builds correctly (npm run build). If you encounter errors, you will need to review the changelogs for those specific packages to update any deprecated APIs.
